# Third-party notices

## DNG technology

This product includes DNG technology under license by Adobe.

Orion implements parts of Adobe's *Digital Negative (DNG) Specification*
(version 1.6.0.0, December 2021) from its published description — the
BaselineExposure zero point (tag 50730) and the HueSatMap profile stage
(tags 50938/50939, ProfileHueSatMapDims/Data/Encoding). The specification
carries a royalty-free patent grant, and that grant requires this notice to
appear prominently in source and documentation.

**No Adobe data is included.** Orion ships no `.dcp` profile from Adobe or from
any project that derives from one. Both values Orion uses are *fitted*, from
the camera's own JPEG and a second independent rendering of the same frame —
the method and the numbers are in `research/camera-profiles.md`. See
`planning/DECISIONS.md` #44 for why redistributing Adobe's profiles is out, and
#45 for an open question about the provenance of LibRaw's built-in matrices.

## LibRaw

Raw decoding uses LibRaw, dual-licensed LGPL-2.1 and CDDL-1.0. Orion links it
dynamically. See `planning/DECISIONS.md` #43.

## OpenCV

Bracket alignment for the HDR merge uses OpenCV (5.x), licensed under the
**Apache License 2.0**. Orion links it dynamically and confines it to one
translation unit (`engine/src/merge/Align.cpp`): ORB feature detection,
Hamming matching, RANSAC homography estimation and ECC refinement.

Copyright the OpenCV team and contributors — <https://opencv.org>.
The full Apache License 2.0 text travels with Orion as `licenses/Apache-2.0.txt`.

## Lens correction database

`data/lensfun/` is the **lensfun** camera and lens database, redistributed under
**Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0)**. The
full licence travels with it, as `data/lensfun/COPYING.CC_BY-SA_3.0`, inside the
application bundle as well as in this repository.

Copyright the lensfun project and its contributors — <https://lensfun.github.io>.
About 1,450 lenses, with their measured distortion and vignetting calibrations.
Orion reads the XML directly and does **not** link the lensfun library, so the
library's LGPL does not apply here; the data's CC BY-SA does.

⚠ **Share-alike binds the data, not Orion.** CC BY-SA 3.0 covers the database
and anything derived from it, so a corrected or extended calibration must be
offered under the same licence — while the application that reads it is
unaffected, exactly as reading a CC BY-SA map does not relicense the reader.
Practically: **fixing a lens entry means contributing it back**, and that is the
right outcome anyway.

## Algorithms implemented from published descriptions

Mathematics is not copyrightable, and none of these is a port of anyone's
source. Each entry in `research/` names its paper.

- RCD-family demosaic — Luis Sanz Rodríguez
- Guided image filtering — He, Sun & Tang
- Starlet (à trous) wavelet denoise — Starck, Fadili & Murtagh
- AgX display transform
- ASC CDL colour grading
- poly3 lens distortion and its autoscale, as lensfun documents the model
- Highlight reconstruction — Masood, Zhu & Tang
- HDR radiance merge weighting — Debevec & Malik; Hasinoff, Durand & Freeman;
  Guillermo Luijk's Zero Noise
- Bracket alignment method — Rublee et al. (ORB); Fischler & Bolles (RANSAC);
  Evangelidis & Psarakis (ECC); via OpenCV, above
- DNG 1.4 floating-point LinearRaw reading and writing — Adobe's published
  specification (see the DNG notice above)

